# The refusal each conformance corpus case has, as our parser
# produces it. `-` is a case that parses clean; anything else is
# the distinct refusal codes it produced, in tree order.
#
# KEYED ON NAME -- `<topic>.md/<case title>`, which is the topic
# file a person named and the heading a person wrote. Neither is a
# POSITION, so a construct moving between tiers is an edit to the
# topic's `**Tier NN name.**` line and leaves every key alone. That
# is the `t/` sweep working, and must not read as a regression.
#
# 213 cases, 207 clean, 6 refusing.
#
# Regenerate with -conformance.update-ratchet and commit the result
# WITH the change that moved it. A baseline updated on its own is a
# number nobody can attribute.
- adjacency-01_literals.md/The whole tier in one body
- adjacency-02_variables.md/The whole tier in one body
- adjacency-03_context.md/The whole tier in one body
trailing_tokens adjacency-04_operators.md/The whole tier in one body
